      text: 'On my first day in London, I wanted to buy a book, so I asked for the library. A kind woman sent me to a building full of people reading quietly — I had to borrow a book instead of buying one! Later, I told my host family that I “pretended” to visit Oxford. They looked confused. Actually, I meant that I intended to go. Eventually, I realized that some words are traps.',
